/-!
# The fpqc sheaf property of the relative Hom and Isom functors, Stacks 08JV and 08K8

In the standing data of Stacks 08JT — a morphism `f : X ⟶ base` of algebraic spaces over a
scheme `S` and two quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-modules `F`, `G` — the relative Hom functor
`Hom(F, G)` of `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Quot/RelativeHom.lean` and its subfunctor
`Isom(F, G)` of `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Quot/RelativeIsom.lean` satisfy the sheaf
property for the fpqc topology.  The reductions of both statements to fpqc descent of
quasi-coherent modules on algebraic spaces were made in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Quot/RelativeHomFpqcDescent.lean` and
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Quot/RelativeIsom.lean`; this file supplies the descent itself,
from Stacks 04W8, and the quasi-coherence of the base-changed modules, from Stacks 03GA, so that
both tags hold under the source's hypotheses alone.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuasiCoherentDescent.DescentDatum.isIso_of_isIso_app`: a morphism of
  descent data whose components are isomorphisms is an isomorphism.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.reflectsIsoAlongFpqcCovering`: a homomorphism of quasi-coherent
  modules whose inverse images along an fpqc covering are isomorphisms is an isomorphism.  This
  is the full-faithfulness clause of Stacks 04W8 read on one morphism, in the form of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ReflectsIsoAlongFpqcCovering`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.HomSituation.isSheafFor_homFunctor_of_isFpqcCovering`:
  **Stacks 08JV**, the sheaf property of `Hom(F, G)` for an fpqc covering of test schemes.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.HomSituation.isSheafFor_isomFunctor_of_isFpqcCovering`:
  **Stacks 08K8**, the sheaf property of `Isom(F, G)` for an fpqc covering of test schemes.

## Implementation notes

As in the files these results complete, there is no fpqc topology on the test schemes over an
algebraic space in this development, so "satisfies the sheaf property for the fpqc topology" is
`CategoryTheory.Presieve.IsSheafFor` for the presieve generated by an arbitrary fpqc covering
family `{T_i ⟶ T}` of test schemes, the covering condition being the fpqc condition of
Stacks 03MQ for the underlying family of algebraic spaces.  Both functors are taken at the
pseudofunctoriality of direct images of Stacks 03LU,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.modulePushforwardCoherence`, which is a theorem.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 08JV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08JV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08K8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08K8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08JT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08JT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03MR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03MR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04W8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04W8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03GA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03GA)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u v

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

namespace QuasiCoherentDescent.DescentDatum

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S} {I : Type v}
  {X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} {Y : I → AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} {f : ∀ i, Y i ⟶ X}

/-- **A morphism of descent data with invertible components is an isomorphism.**  The
componentwise inverses commute with the pairwise isomorphisms because the components do, so they
form a morphism of descent data, inverse to the given one. -/
theorem isIso_of_isIso_app {D E : DescentDatum B S hS Y f} (a : D ⟶ E)
    [∀ i, IsIso (a.app i)] : IsIso a := by
  refine ⟨⟨⟨fun i ↦ inv (a.app i), fun i j ↦ ?_⟩, ?_, ?_⟩⟩
  · rw [Functor.map_inv, Functor.map_inv, IsIso.inv_comp_eq, ← Category.assoc,
      a.naturality i j, Category.assoc, IsIso.hom_inv_id, Category.comp_id]
  · exact Hom.ext fun i ↦ IsIso.hom_inv_id (a.app i)
  · exact Hom.ext fun i ↦ IsIso.inv_hom_id (a.app i)

end QuasiCoherentDescent.DescentDatum

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S}

open QuasiCoherentDescent in
/-- **Invertibility of a homomorphism of quasi-coherent modules descends along an fpqc
covering**, the full-faithfulness clause of Stacks 04W8 read on one morphism: a homomorphism of
quasi-coherent modules whose inverse images along the members of an fpqc covering are all
isomorphisms is an isomorphism.

The canonical descent functor of the covering sends the homomorphism to a morphism of descent
data with invertible components, hence to an isomorphism; that functor is an equivalence by
Stacks 04W8, `QuasiCoherentDescent.isEquivalence_canonicalDescentFunctor'_of_isFpqcCovering`,
so it reflects isomorphisms. -/
theorem reflectsIsoAlongFpqcCovering : ReflectsIsoAlongFpqcCovering.{u, v} B S hS := by
  intro I W Z p hp M N hM hN φ hφ
  have := isEquivalence_canonicalDescentFunctor'_of_isFpqcCovering B S hS Z p hp
  let M' : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS W.1 W.2 := ⟨M, hM⟩
  let N' : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS W.1 W.2 := ⟨N, hN⟩
  let φ' : M' ⟶ N' := ObjectProperty.homMk φ
  have : ∀ i, IsIso (((canonicalDescentFunctor' B S hS Z p).map φ').app i) := hφ
  have : IsIso ((canonicalDescentFunctor' B S hS Z p).map φ') :=
    DescentDatum.isIso_of_isIso_app _
  have : IsIso φ' := isIso_of_reflects_iso φ' (canonicalDescentFunctor' B S hS Z p)
  exact (inferInstance : IsIso ((ObjectProperty.ι _).map φ'))

namespace HomSituation

variable (s : HomSituation B S hS)

/-- The fpqc sheaf property of the relative Hom functor (the content of Stacks 08JV; this lemma
is the input 08K8 needs).  In Situation 08JT the relative Hom functor `Hom(F, G)` satisfies the
sheaf property for the fpqc topology: for every fpqc covering `{U i ⟶ T}` of schemes over the
base, every compatible family of homomorphisms `F_{U i} ⟶ G_{U i}` has a unique amalgamation
`F_T ⟶ G_T`.

This is the proof of the source.  The base changes `{X_{U i} ⟶ X_T}` form an fpqc covering of
`X_T` by Stacks 03MR, and a compatible family of homomorphisms of quasi-coherent modules glues
uniquely along it by Stacks 04W8, `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.gluesModuleHomAlongFpqcCovering`;
the base-changed modules `F_T`, `G_T` are quasi-coherent by Stacks 03GA,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_modulePullback_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite`. -/
theorem isSheafFor_homFunctor_of_isFpqcCovering {I : Type v} {T : s.SchemesOver}
    {U : I → s.SchemesOver} (g : ∀ i, U i ⟶ T)
    (hg : IsFpqcCovering B S hS fun i ↦ ((schemeSpaceFunctor B S hS).map (g i).left).hom) :
    Presieve.IsSheafFor (s.homFunctor (modulePushforwardCoherence B S hS))
      (Presieve.ofArrows U g) :=
  s.isSheafFor_homFunctor (modulePushforwardCoherence B S hS) g hg

/-- **Stacks 08K8.**  In Situation 08JT the relative Isom functor `Isom(F, G)` satisfies the
sheaf property for the fpqc topology: for every fpqc covering `{U i ⟶ T}` of schemes over the
base, every compatible family of invertible homomorphisms `F_{U i} ⟶ G_{U i}` has a unique
amalgamation, an invertible homomorphism `F_T ⟶ G_T`.

This is the proof of the source.  `Hom(F, G)` satisfies the sheaf property, Stacks 08JV in the
form of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.HomSituation.isSheafFor_homFunctor_of_isFpqcCovering`, so it
remains that a homomorphism `F_T ⟶ G_T` whose base changes to the `U i` are isomorphisms is an
isomorphism; the base changes `{X_{U i} ⟶ X_T}` form an fpqc covering of `X_T` by Stacks 03MR,
and invertibility descends along it by Stacks 04W8,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.reflectsIsoAlongFpqcCovering`, the base-changed modules being
quasi-coherent by Stacks 03GA. -/
@[stacks 08K8 "the functor Isom(F, G) of Situation 08JT satisfies the sheaf property for \
every fpqc covering"]
theorem isSheafFor_isomFunctor_of_isFpqcCovering {I : Type v} {T : s.SchemesOver}
    {U : I → s.SchemesOver} (g : ∀ i, U i ⟶ T)
    (hg : IsFpqcCovering B S hS fun i ↦ ((schemeSpaceFunctor B S hS).map (g i).left).hom) :
    Presieve.IsSheafFor s.isomFunctor (Presieve.ofArrows U g) :=
  s.isSheafFor_isomFunctor (reflectsIsoAlongFpqcCovering.{u, v}) g hg
    (isQuasicoherentOnSite_modulePullback_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite B S hS (s.projection T)
      s.F s.quasicoherent_F)
    (isQuasicoherentOnSite_modulePullback_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite B S hS (s.projection T)
      s.G s.quasicoherent_G)
    (s.isSheafFor_homFunctor_of_isFpqcCovering g hg)

end HomSituation

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
